Many thanks to Nikola Milutinovic, Olle Eriksson and Brusche, Johan.

As you may recall I have a factory-new ES45 running 5.1B with 1st patch.
My problem was dxadvfs not starting and simply returning 1 as $status
(Of course I have ADVFS-UTILITIES pak installed).

With the help of HPQDEC people I discoverd a log fine 
/var/advfs/gui/advfs_gui.log which had some errors:

 Mon Mar 10 10:23:38 CET 2003 | ERROR | File open failed. | File app_hostlist.c | Line 428
 Mon Mar 10 10:23:38 CET 2003 | ERROR | A system error occurred: No 
 message of desired type
 | File app_hostlist.c | Line 430
 Mon Mar 10 10:23:38 CET 2003 | ERROR | File open failed. | File
 app_hostlist.c | Line 428
 Mon Mar 10 10:23:38 CET 2003 | ERROR | A system error occurred: No
 message of desired type
 | File app_hostlist.c | Line 430
 Exiting due to fatal error.
 Mon Mar 10 10:23:38 CET 2003 | INFO | Exiting due to fatal error.
 | File app_init.c | Line 451

The above message couldn't help but I recalled several years ago I had a
problem with vdump/vrestore related with the value of the $LANG
environment variable. I use tcsh and in .cshrc of any machine of mine I
set
	LANG=en_US.ISO8859-1
Of course the same was on the new ES45.

So I tried to 
	unset LANG 
and soon after, MAGICALLY dxadvfs started as supposed to do !!!

>From that moment on, dxadvfs starts properly reguardless the value or
the existance of the $LANG environment variable !!

So I solved such a very strange problem!

Hoping my work can be usefull to some other alphist,
Ciao to everybody from Italy,

Emanuele

