Many thanks to Dr Tom Blinn and Johan Brusche,

There are some good reasons to preserve the original cluster creation 
disk from the standalone system, but if you choose to re-use it, then 
you should remove the domain entries from /etc/fdmns since there are 
things both in the kernel and in user space that can get confused by 
domain definitions in that directory that point to disks that don't 
have the domains implied by the entries. 

Tom 


You can safely remove these dirs and links in /etc/fdmns. 
Note: You should consider making a backup of these, it greatly 
reduces the time required to reconstruct your cluster in case of 
disaster. 

Johan. 

Thanks to all


