Problem: Unsupported hardware detected on systems using KZPCC controllers.

Summary:

The installupdate script incorrectly reports that the KZPCC driver is unsupported.

Apparently, it parses the bus and controller names, truncating them at the first digit
so the KZPCC driver i2o becomes i, which it then fails to recognise as a supported
device.

After ignoring the warning and continuing the installation, 5.1B successfully
install and runs on this hardware.

Thanks to Dr Thomas Blinn & Randy Rodgers.


Original question:

> I have a DS20E with a KZPCC controller, currently running Tru64 UNIX 5.1A PK3.
> Firmware is the latest.
> 
> While attempting to upgrade to Tru64 UNIX 5.1B the following message was
> displayed indicating the hardware (about 5 months old) is not supported in the
> new release.  Any ideas why?  I have succesfully installed 5.1B on several
> other machines that are 4 or 5 years old.
> 
> 
> *** START UPDATE INSTALLATION (Mon Mar 3 14:52:31 EST 2003) ***
>     FLAGS:
> 
> 
> Checking for retired hardware...done.
> 
> 
> The following hardware has been detected on your system.  The update
> installation process has determined that this hardware is not
> supported in the new release (Compaq Computer Corporation Tru64 UNIX
> V5.1B).  If you continue with the update installation this hardware
> will no longer function once the operating system has been updated.
> The loss of this hardware may make the system unusable.  It is
> recommended that you do not continue with the update installation.
> 
> i
> 
> For further information on retired hardware see the Release Notes for
> Compaq Computer Corporation Tru64 UNIX V5.1B.
> 
> Do you want to continue the Update Installation? (y/n) [n]: n
