Wow, blindingly fast reply from Mary Aumann <MJA@svsu.edu> who is out of
the office :-).

Seriously: Thanks to Voetelink D. <voetelink@ecn.nl> who reminded me to
get ahold of the MIBs from the Insight manager. If found the mibs under
/usr/share/sysman/mibs and also figured out how to use the table walk
feature of snmp_request. So that:

$ /usr/sbin/snmp_request localhost public getnext -t 1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.2.2.1.8.3
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.1.0 = 1
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.3.0 = 1
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.4.1.1.1 = 1
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.4.1.5.1 = 1
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.4.1.10.1 = 1
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.4.1.11.1 = 1
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.5.1.1.1 = 1
1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.5.1.2.1 = 2

finally pointed me to 1.3.6.1.4.1.36.2.18.22.1.8.3.5.1.2.1 where 2 means
that the power supply is good.

Thanks again // Tom

