With tanks to Mr.Blinn who mentioned:
"If it's a problem with the firmware in the FDDI card and there
is an update, the update would be (I believe) applied by doing
a firmware update on the system, that is, update the SRM from
the more up to date firmware update media...." =20

He also pointed to the right choice of the Firmware version.
As he said "...update to a version that's been tested with V4.0F".

He told me another potential responsible for this error:
"The symptoms could also be a result of whatever the fibre goes
to in your network -- if you've got a flaky fibre router, for
example, it could cause these same problems.  Don't assume that
just because they are being reported in the UNIX system that
they are a fault in the UNIX system, they may just be reports
of problems on the backbone network."

Here we are at the moment.=20

