So it comes , thank you to Geoff Allen [geoff@wsu.edu]

We are using it with a milter (spamassassin_milter, 
http://www.runestig.com/osp.html#SA-MILTER, but other milters should work 
as well).

With the milter, all mail gets scanned, incoming, outgoing, local users, 
remote users, etc.

The spamassassin_milter.c source file has a comment at the top that 
explains the basic idea.

Yes, you do add some information to sendmail.cf (or sendmail.mc). You then 
start the milter, which opens a socket file that the milter uses to 
communicate with it. You'll need to change your sendmail startup to start 
spamd and start the milter before you start sendmail.

So it's running.

